.TH CTPOOL_TIMED_SUBMIT 3 "2026-10-01" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ctpool_timed_submit \- submit a task with a timeout
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadpool.h>

ccol_retval_t ctpool_timed_submit(ctpool pool,
                                  void (*fn)(void *),
                                  void *arg,
                                  void (*on_complete)(void *arg, bool ran),
                                  uint64_t timeout_us);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Works like ctpool_submit, except that for a bounded queue it waits at
most timeout_us microseconds for a free slot, measured from the call.
The library converts the timeout to an absolute deadline with
CLOCK_MONOTONIC, so a change to the wall clock of the system (by an
administrator, NTP, or the resume of a virtual machine) does not make
the wait longer or shorter.

A timeout_us of 0 makes this call the same as ctpool_try_submit, which
does not wait.

A timeout too large to form a deadline, such as UINT64_MAX, waits for as
long as the queue stays full: the deadline saturates at the latest
representable time and never wraps into the past.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
pool         Thread pool handle
fn           Task function (must not be NULL)
arg          The library gives it to fn and on_complete (may be NULL)
on_complete  Called once for the task: on_complete(arg, true) after
             fn returns, or on_complete(arg, false) when the pool
             discards the task unrun (may be NULL)
timeout_us   Longest time to wait, in microseconds (0 = do not wait)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success           - task enqueued.
ccol_invalid_args      - pool is CTPOOL_INVALID or a stale/already-
                         destroyed handle, or fn is NULL.
ccol_not_enough_memory - task struct allocation failed.
ccol_not_permitted     - pool is shutting down.
ccol_container_full    - timeout_us is 0 and the queue is full.
ccol_timed_out         - timeout elapsed before a slot became free.
ccol_unexpected_failure - clock_gettime or pthread_cond_timedwait
                          returned an unexpected error.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ctpool_submit (3),
.BR ctpool_try_submit (3)
